<!--
  Free narrative fragment: rotation convention flip diagram (A1)
  Shows the before/after matrix entries for rotateX and rotateY,
  and the expected CCW test values that must pass post-fix.
-->
<div style="font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 700px; margin: 1.5rem 0; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; background: var(--surface-1, #f8fafc); border: 1px solid var(--border, #e2e8f0); border-radius: 8px;">
  <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.75rem; font-size: 1rem;">A1 — Rotation convention flip (CCW right-handed)</h3>

  <p style="margin: 0 0 0.75rem; font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--text-2, #475569);">
    All three axes use the right-handed CCW convention: looking <em>down</em> the positive axis toward the origin, positive angles rotate counter-clockwise.
  </p>

  <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
    <div>
      <strong style="font-size: 0.8125rem; display: block; margin-bottom: 0.4rem; color: var(--danger, #dc2626);">rotateX — BEFORE (wrong)</strong>
      <pre style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.8rem; background: #fff; border: 1px solid #fca5a5; border-radius: 4px; padding: 0.5rem;">newY = pZ·sin + pY·cos  ← wrong
newZ = pZ·cos − pY·sin  ← wrong

Test: Point(0,1,0).rotateX(π/2)
  → (0, 1, 0)  ✗ (should be (0,0,1))</pre>
    </div>
    <div>
      <strong style="font-size: 0.8125rem; display: block; margin-bottom: 0.4rem; color: var(--ok, #16a34a);">rotateX — AFTER (correct)</strong>
      <pre style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.8rem; background: #fff; border: 1px solid #86efac; border-radius: 4px; padding: 0.5rem;">newY = pY·cos − pZ·sin  ← correct
newZ = pY·sin + pZ·cos  ← correct

Test: Point(0,1,0).rotateX(π/2)
  → (0, 0, 1)  ✓</pre>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1rem;">
    <div>
      <strong style="font-size: 0.8125rem; display: block; margin-bottom: 0.4rem; color: var(--danger, #dc2626);">rotateY — BEFORE (wrong)</strong>
      <pre style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.8rem; background: #fff; border: 1px solid #fca5a5; border-radius: 4px; padding: 0.5rem;">newX = pX·cos − pZ·sin
newZ = pX·sin + pZ·cos

Test: Point(0,0,1).rotateY(π/2)
  → (0, 0, 1)  ✗ (should be (1,0,0))</pre>
    </div>
    <div>
      <strong style="font-size: 0.8125rem; display: block; margin-bottom: 0.4rem; color: var(--ok, #16a34a);">rotateY — AFTER (correct)</strong>
      <pre style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.8rem; background: #fff; border: 1px solid #86efac; border-radius: 4px; padding: 0.5rem;">newX = pZ·sin + pX·cos
newZ = pZ·cos − pX·sin

Test: Point(0,0,1).rotateY(π/2)
  → (1, 0, 0)  ✓</pre>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p style="margin: 0.75rem 0 0; font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-2, #475569);">
    <strong>rotateZ</strong> (already correct): newX = pX·cos − pY·sin; newY = pX·sin + pY·cos.
    Test: Point(1,0,0).rotateZ(π/2) → (0,1,0). This test already passes; it must continue to pass after the fix.
  </p>
</div>
